# An unclosed `[` before `;`: DS0112 points at it; the next statement parses.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | extend x = tags[0;
from 'customers.csv' | count
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..68
  PIPELINE@0..37
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    EXTEND_OP@20..37
      IDENT@20..26 "extend"
      WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@27..37
        NAME@27..28
          IDENT@27..28 "x"
        WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
        EQ@29..30 "="
        WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
        INDEX_EXPR@31..37
          NAME_REF@31..35
            IDENT@31..35 "tags"
          L_BRACK@35..36 "["
          LITERAL@36..37
            LONG@36..37 "0"
  SEMICOLON@37..38 ";"
  WHITESPACE@38..39 "\n"
  PIPELINE@39..67
    IDENT@39..43 "from"
    WHITESPACE@43..44 " "
    LITERAL@44..59
      STRING@44..59 "'customers.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@59..60 " "
    PIPE@60..61 "|"
    WHITESPACE@61..62 " "
    COUNT_OP@62..67
      IDENT@62..67 "count"
  WHITESPACE@67..68 "\n"

error[DS0112]: unclosed `[`
  --> query:1:36
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | extend x = tags[0;
  |                                    ^ - expected `]` before this
  |                                    |
  |                                    this `[` is never closed
  |
  = help: add `]` where the bracketed part ends
